-q
----------------------------------------------------------------------
' INP applies the mask to the value read from the address. Two const masks
' are special: 0 leaves nothing of the value, and 177777 keeps all of it,
' so the compiler warns about both. A mask in a variable is not const and
' gives no warning.
10 A% = INP(1000, 255)
20 A% = INP(1000, 0)
30 A% = INP(1000, &HFFFF)
40 A% = INP(1000, 65535)
50 B% = 255
60 A% = INP(1000, B%)
' The address and the mask can be Single, then the compiler converts them to
' Integer with FTOI. A Single const mask is folded the same as an Integer one.
70 A% = INP(1000.0, 255)
80 F = 1000.0
90 A% = INP(F, 255)
100 A% = INP(1000, 15.0)
110 G = 15.0
120 A% = INP(1000, G)
130 A% = INP(1000, 0.0)
140 A% = INP(1000.0, 65535.0)
----------------------------------------------------------------------
